## 5. Escalation handlers

**Directory:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/`. Each YAML maps an exception class (the filename) to a handler class. All 9:

| YAML file (exception) | Handler class |
|---|---|
| `...escalation.NotFoundException.yml` | `NotFoundExceptionHandler` |
| `...escalation.OwnerTelephoneInUseException.yml` | `OwnerTelephoneInUseExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.dao.DataIntegrityViolationException.yml` | `DataIntegrityViolationExceptionHandler` |
| `java.lang.Exception.yml` | `GeneralExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.web.bind.MethodArgumentNotValidException.yml` | `ValidationExceptionHandler` |
| `...escalation.OwnerFieldsInvalidException.yml` | `OwnerFieldsInvalidExceptionHandler` |
| `...escalation.OwnerCityAtCapacityException.yml` | `OwnerCityAtCapacityExceptionHandler` |
| `...escalation.OwnerHouseholdConflictException.yml` | `OwnerHouseholdConflictExceptionHandler` |
| `org.springframework.security.authorization.AuthorizationDeniedException.yml` | `ForbiddenExceptionHandler` |

Each YAML has the same shape, e.g.:
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.OwnerFieldsInvalidExceptionHandler
```

Handler Java classes live in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/`. Two examples:

`OwnerFieldsInvalidExceptionHandler.java` (→ 400):
```java
public class OwnerFieldsInvalidExceptionHandler {
    public void handle(@Parameter OwnerFieldsInvalidException ex,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>>> response) {
        response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)
                .body(Map.of("errors", ex.getErrors())));
    }
}
```

`OwnerTelephoneInUseExceptionHandler.java` (→ 409):
```java
public class OwnerTelephoneInUseExceptionHandler {
    public void handle(@Parameter OwnerTelephoneInUseException ex,
            ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<Map<String, Object>>> response) {
        response.send(ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CONFLICT)
                .body(Map.of("error", ex.getMessage())));
    }
}
```

Handler pattern: `handle(@Parameter <Exception> ex, ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<...>> response)`. The exception classes themselves (`OwnerFieldsInvalidException` carrying `List<String> errors`; `OwnerTelephoneInUseException` carrying `telephone`) also live in this package.

## 6. Tests related to owner creation

Only three test files exist, all under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`. They are black-box acceptance tests that POST to `/api/owners`.

**AcceptanceBase.java** — the harness. `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(username="acceptance-admin", roles={"OWNER_ADMIN","VET_ADMIN","ADMIN"})`. Key helpers:
- `createOwner(JsonNode body)` → `mvc.perform(post("/api/owners").contentType(APPLICATION_JSON).content(json(body)))`
- `createOwnerOk(body)` → asserts 2xx, returns id via `extractId` (reads `id` from body or the `Location` header)
- `createOwnerWithKey(body, key)` → POST with `Idempotency-Key` header
- `ownerNode()` → a fully-unique valid owner (firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city/telephone); `withPostcode`, `structuredOwner`, `knownOwner(city)` variants
- `fillCity(city, n)`, `createMany(n)` bulk helpers; `getOwner(id)`, `fetchOwner(id)`, `deleteOwner(id)`
- Reference data maps (CITY_REGION, REGION_TIMEZONE, REGION_POSTCODES, HOLIDAYS) and algorithms (`sha256hex`, `shaHex`, `luhn`) for asserting derived values.

**AcceptanceTest.java** — one concrete test:
```java
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test
    void coreRejectsOverDailyLimit() throws Exception {
        createMany(100);
        createOwner(ownerNode()).andExpect(status().isTooManyRequests());
    }
}
```
(Creates 100 owners dated today, expects the 101st POST /api/owners to be 429.)

**AuditLogCapture.java** — a test support helper (audit-log capture), not itself a POST test.

Note: tests exercise the endpoint end-to-end through MockMvc (both OfficeFloor and Spring arms), not the individual function classes directly.

## 7. Request/response DTOs

The DTOs used are **`OwnerFieldsDto`** (request body) and **`OwnerDto`** (response), in package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`. These are **generated at build time**, not checked into source — the openapi-generator-maven-plugin generates them from `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` with `modelNameSuffix = Dto` and `modelPackage = ...rest.dto`. (`target/` is not currently built, so no `.java` files exist on disk.)

Schema source in `openapi.yml`:

**`OwnerFields`** (→ `OwnerFieldsDto`, the request) — properties: `firstName` (1–30, pattern letters/space/'/-), `lastName` (1–30, similar pattern, optional trailing dot), `address` (1–255), `city` (1–80), `telephone` (1–20, pattern `^[+0-9 ()-]+$`, stored E.164), `email` (format email, optional, stored lower-cased), `registrationDate` (format date, optional; defaults to server current date), `sharesHousehold` (boolean, `writeOnly`). Required: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone.

**`Owner`** (→ `OwnerDto`, the response) — `allOf` OwnerFields plus read-only: `id` (int32), `displayName` ("Last, First"), `initials` ("G.F."), `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `householdId`, `namesakeCount` (int32), `membershipTier` (enum SILVER/BRONZE), `locality`. These read-only/derived fields are populated by `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`.

## 8. Build file — officefloor starter & running tests

**Path:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (Maven; Spring Boot parent `4.1.0`, `officefloor.version = 4.0.2`).

OfficeFloor starter dependency:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>net.officefloor.springboot</groupId>
    <artifactId>officefloor-rest-spring-boot-4-starter</artifactId>
    <version>${officefloor.version}</version>
</dependency>
```
Test-scoped OfficeFloor testing dependency:
```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>net.officefloor.web</groupId>
    <artifactId>woof_test</artifactId>
    <version>${officefloor.version}</version>
    <scope>test</scope>
</dependency>
```

**Running tests:** standard Maven Surefire via the Spring Boot parent — `mvn test` (or `mvn verify`). Tests use `spring-boot-starter-test`, `spring-boot-starter-webmvc-test` (MockMvc), `spring-boot-starter-security-test`, `mockito-core`, and `json-path`, all test-scoped.

Build-time code generation relevant to this endpoint:
- **openapi-generator-maven-plugin** generates the API interfaces and `*Dto` models from `openapi.yml` (generatorName `spring`, `interfaceOnly=true`, `modelNameSuffix=Dto`, model package `...rest.dto`, api package `...rest.api`).
- **build-helper-maven-plugin** adds `target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java` as a source root.
- **maven-compiler-plugin** runs the MapStruct processor (`mapstruct.defaultComponentModel=spring`) to implement `OwnerMapper`.
- **jacoco** enforces coverage (line ≥ 0.85, branch ≥ 0.66) but excludes generated `rest/dto/**` and `rest/api/**`.

One nuance worth flagging: `BuildOwner`/`AssignCustomerCode` produce a `customerCode` like `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, but the `openapi.yml` description of `customerCode` says `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and `membershipNumber` example `SMI-0007-M26` — the code includes a city prefix that the spec text omits.
